 "deadbolts": "Smart deadbolts: arched & slim",
 "lock2": "Smart deadbolts: keypad & glass",
 "airsensors:intro": "Sixteen air-quality and climate sensors, from simple light-bar boxes to e-ink and LED-dot monitors, on desks, shelves and walls. The slider is air quality: high is good (green), middle is fair (yellow), low is poor (orange, red). Each one shows it its own way: a light bar, a color ring, segment numbers, LED dots or a comfort face.",
 "consoles:intro": "Block-style consoles from the original big black box to the newest black tower, plus two classic 90s consoles, drawn at real proportions with their controllers. When playing, the power light comes on, the jewel and the tower's top vent glow green, the memory card screen lights up, and the TV washes the wall.",
 "consoles2:intro": "Every console in this family from the first gray disc box to the newest striped tower, drawn from press photos at real proportions with that era's controller. When playing, the real light comes on: green power lights on the first three, the white light bar on the wedge models and the edge strips on the wing towers, plus controller lights, while the TV washes the wall.",
 "consoles3:intro": "Every home console in this family from the 8-bit gray box to the newest hybrid, in release order, drawn from photos at real proportions with their controllers. When playing, the power light comes on, the disc slot glows, handheld and tablet screens show original game scenery, and the TV washes the wall.",
 "speakers2:intro": "Twenty voice-assistant devices drawn from real shapes, from the first tall speaker to the wall control panel. Listening lights the cyan-on-blue ring or light bar and the screens show a clock, weather, photo or home card; the slider is volume, shown as the ring filling white. The color is the device's real finish.",
 "speakers:intro": "Twenty smart home devices on shelves, counters, walls and doors: speakers, smart displays, streamers, mesh Wi-Fi, thermostats, a smoke alarm, cameras, the doorbell, a deadbolt and a plug-in hub. On shows the four breathing dots, ambient screens and status lights; the slider sets volume. The cameras show Live, Recording, Motion, Privacy or Offline with a Night IR menu, the doorbell has its own State menu, the deadbolt shows Locking, Unlocking and Jammed, and the round thermostat adds Mode.",
 "deadbolts:intro": "Electronic deadbolts and levers by model and trim (arched, slim, round and square), redrawn from product photos (outside face only, no logos). On means LOCKED: bolt out, check or padlock lit green, keypad backlit; off means UNLOCKED: bolt in, status dim red. The color is that model's real finishes. The State menu also shows Locking and Unlocking (bolt part-way, amber light, arrows) and Jammed (red warning light and badge).",
 "lock2:intro": "Smart deadbolts with glass touchscreens and keypads, redrawn from product photos (outside face only, no logos): keyed and key-free, slim and lever versions, a retrofit, a smart-standard lock, an entrance handle lock and a handleset. On means LOCKED: bolt out, check lit green, digits backlit; off means UNLOCKED: bolt in, red status. The color is that model's real finishes. The State menu also shows Locking and Unlocking (bolt part-way, amber light, arrows) and Jammed (red warning light and badge).",
 "countertop:intro": "Real countertop ovens and food warmers. When cooking, the elements glow orange behind the glass, air-fry fans swirl, the rotisserie turns, steam rises and warmer lamps glow; the display shows the temperature (the slider sets it). Warmers let you pick the food; the stacked double oven runs each oven on its own and the flip-up oven can be flipped up.",
 "floorcare:intro": "Twenty vacuums and carpet cleaners: stick vacuums with laser heads, uprights, lift-aways, wet-dry floor washers, carpet cleaners, a rental-style deep cleaner, canisters, a handheld and a shop vac. Cleaning spins the brush roll, swirls the bin, lights the head and shows the battery; the slider sets power.",
 "fridge:intro": "Twenty fridge styles: 4-door flex panels and a screen fridge, knock-glass and color-glow French doors, plus classic top and bottom freezers, side-by-sides, a counter-depth French door and built-in columns. Running shows the dispenser light, displays, the door screen and lit glass panels; the slider sets display brightness.",
 "home4:intro": "Server racks for the home lab (8U open frame, 12U glass wall cabinet, 42U mesh cabinet, 25U 4-post rack, 10-inch mini rack, 4-bay NAS) and desk monitors (27-inch office, 34-inch curved, 49-inch super-wide, aluminum 27-inch, a portable screen). On racks the slider is activity: more port and drive lights blink, faster. On monitors it is screen brightness.",
 "laundry:intro": "Eighteen washers and dryers. Pick a cycle on each one: washers fill, wash in soapy water, rinse in clear water, spin with the clothes pressed to the drum, then finish; dryers tumble with a warm glow, then cool down. The screen or display shows the cycle and the time left (the slider sets it). Pairs and stacks switch the washer and dryer on their own.",
 "outlets:intro": "In-wall outlets: hidden-plug outlets (plain, light ring, USB-C, USB-C with ring) plus common outlets from a plain duplex to GFCI, smart, floor and pop-up types. On means power on: LEDs and night-lights glow, a plug is in and its lamp is lit. The color is the plate or finish (the light on light-ring models). Split outlets show each plug with its cord, so you can see which half is on.",
 "printers:intro": "Thirteen home and office printers plus seven 3D printers on a desk (the four filament printers follow the approved lineup drawing). While printing, a page slides out (color pages from color printers, text from mono ones), the inkjet carriage runs back and forth and the status light blinks. The slider is the ink or toner level: on the gauges and the ink-tank windows, and below 25% everything turns amber. On 3D printers the slider is print progress: the part grows, the head moves, the bed glows and the resin plate lifts.",
 "switch:intro": "Twenty wall switches, dimmers and keypads on painted walls. On flips each one to its ON position and lights its status LED in the LED color; dimmers fill their LED bar to the brightness. Plates come in white, ivory, almond, black, stainless, brass and glass by model. Gangs makes 1 to 4 of the same switch on one plate (each gang can follow its own entity), Role picks Main or Aux, and some dimmers let you pick the Control (paddle, rotary, slide or touch).",
 "utility2:intro": "Seventeen real boilers, heat pumps, circulators, buffer tanks and fresh-water stations in basements and utility rooms. On means running: displays light, flow moves in the pipes, pumps spin and flues shimmer. The slider is the output: temperatures, gauges and readouts follow it. The wall combi boiler has separate Heating and Hot water switches.",
